<title>SLOVAKIA: MOL opens its first Slovak gas station.</title>
<headline>MOL opens its first Slovak gas station.</headline>
<dateline>NOVE ZAMKY, Slovakia 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian oil and gas company MOL on Friday opened its first gas station in Slovakia as a part of its expansion strategy in central and eastern Europe, MOL officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our goal is to be one of the top five retailers in Slovakia,&quot; MOL General Manager Zoltan Mandoki told Reuters after the opening ceremony at Nove Zamky, near the Hungarian-Slovak border.</p>
<p>MOL has already had four petrol stations in Romania and in Ukraine and planned to expand the Romanian and Slovak retail network as quickly as possible, Mandoki said.</p>
<p>He added that MOL's future plans also include opening outlets in Slovenia and Croatia and, as the political situation stabilises, in Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>-- Denes Albert, Budapest nesroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
